    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9327" root="حنف" body-key="H">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِفَ</span></b> , (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنْفٌ</span>, (TK,) <i>He,</i>
or <i>it, inclined,</i> or <i>declined.</i> (K, TA.) You say,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفَ إِلَيْهِ</span> (TA) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اليه</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تحنّف</span></b>  (K) <i>He inclined
to it.</i> (K, TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفَ عَنْهُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عنه</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تحنّف</span></b> 
<i>He declined from it.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِفَ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفَ</span></b> ,
(Msb, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفٌ</span>; (Msb;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنُفَ</span>,
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنُفَ</span></b> ; (K;) <i>He had that kind of distortion
which is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَفٌ</span> <i>as explained below.</i>
(Msb, K.)

